.TH EUCLID-CLI-EMO-LIST-ALERT-RULES 1 "October 2026" "euclid-cli 2.1.3" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-emo-list-alert-rules \- list the threshold alert rules
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli emo list-alert-rules
[\fB\-\-rule\-id\fR|\fB\-r\fR \fIID\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists the account's alert rules, by id, each with everything it was
created with: the metric, the label selector, the statistic, the
comparison, the lines, the period counts, whether it is enabled, and when
it was created and last changed. A line the rule does not have is
.IR null .
.PP
What a rule is judging right now is
.BR euclid-cli-emo-list-alerts (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rule\-id " " \fIID\fR
Only this rule.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The rules were printed as JSON
.RI ( "{items}" ).
.TP
.B 1
The caller was not authenticated, or is not an administrator.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli emo list-alert-rules
euclid-cli emo list-alert-rules --rule-id system-cpu-per-host
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-emo (1),
.BR euclid-cli-emo-create-alert-rule (1),
.BR euclid-cli-emo-list-alerts (1)
